<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Automatic Scooter Short vs Long-Term Rental Cost in Hanoi: Cost Planning</h1>
<p>An automatic scooter in Hanoi rents on fully published ladders in two tiers: the entry tier at 150,000 VND per day, 700,000 VND per week and 900,000 to 1,200,000 VND per month, and the step-up tier at 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week and 1,500,000 to 2,000,000 VND per month. This guide compares short-term against long-term cost so the calendar, not habit, picks the rate.</p>
<p>We put both ladders side by side, find the break-even points at five days and around ten days, show what each structure is actually for, and close with the deposit, gear and support questions that long stays add. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, see the full model range at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and check common questions on the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The two verified ladders</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">What short-term cost looks like</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">What long-term cost looks like</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The break-even at five days</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">The break-even at ten days</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">Riding an automatic short versus long</a></li>
